  <p>
    Your password manager should be ready when you need it. Open a login form,
    find your password, switch back to the other app, grab a verification code.
    That ordinary sequence should not mean typing your master password over and over.
  </p>
  <p>
    The new <strong>Authier for Android</strong> brings your passwords and
    authenticator codes to a native app built for your phone. It supports offline
    vault access, Android Autofill, trusted-device approval, and fingerprint unlock.
    You can install the signed <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier/releases/tag/v0.1.3-android">Android 0.1.3 release</a>
    today on Android 8 or newer.
  </p>

