  <h2>A lock timer that does what you choose</h2>
  <p>
    Set the timeout to 15 minutes, leave Authier to use another app, and come back:
    your vault stays unlocked while that inactivity window is still open.
    Closing the app, force-stopping it, or restarting your phone does not reset
    your choice or force an early vault lock.
  </p>
  <p>
    In <strong>Settings → Automatic lock</strong>, choose 1, 5, 15, or 30 minutes;
    1, 4, 8, or 12 hours; or a full day. The choice saves on your phone and works
    offline. Activity in the app renews the timer; reopening it by itself does not.
    Once the selected period without activity has passed, the vault locks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prefer to lock whenever you leave? That option is still there. You can also
    tap <strong>Lock vault</strong> at any time to lock immediately, regardless
    of the timeout.
  </p>

  <h2>Unlock with your fingerprint</h2>
  <p>
    After unlocking your vault, open <strong>Settings → Fingerprint unlock</strong>
    and enable it. Android asks you to confirm with an enrolled fingerprint or
    another supported strong biometric. If you have not registered one yet,
    Authier takes you to Android’s enrollment settings; return to the app afterward
    to finish enabling the feature.
  </p>
  <p>
    The next time your vault locks, tap <strong>Unlock with fingerprint</strong>.
    Your master password remains available as a fallback. Android performs the
    biometric check—Authier never receives or stores your fingerprint data.
    Changing the fingerprints registered on your phone requires setting up
    Authier’s biometric unlock again with your master password.
  </p>

  <h2>Passwords and codes, even offline</h2>
  <p>
    Search your saved logins, create and edit passwords, generate a new password,
    and copy a verification code from the authenticator tab. Once your vault is
    on the phone, you can unlock and use it without an internet connection.
  </p>
  <p>
    Edits made offline stay encrypted on the device and sync when you reconnect
    and sync the vault. If another device changed the same item, Authier lets you
    review the conflict and preserve the value you need before discarding a local
    change. Your phone also joins the same <a href="/guides/trusted-device-approval">trusted-device approval flow</a>
    as the browser extension.
  </p>

  <h2>Fill a login without copying it around</h2>
  <p>
    Enable <strong>Android Autofill</strong> in Authier’s settings. In a supported
    native app’s login form, choose a saved account and confirm
    <strong>Use login and fill</strong>. Authier remembers the app association
    so linked logins appear first next time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Autofill uses the same timed unlock session. While the session is valid,
    you can go straight to choosing an account. After it expires, unlock with
    your fingerprint or master password. You still choose which login to fill.
    This release supports native app forms; embedded browser forms and Android
    passkey authentication are not supported yet.
  </p>

  <h2>Native Android, the same encrypted vault</h2>
  <p>
    We built this app with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose and retired the old React
    Native mobile project. The new client uses Authier’s existing encrypted vault
    format, so your passwords and codes can travel between your browser and phone.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your master password and decrypted vault items are not saved to disk. To make
    timed and fingerprint unlock possible, the app saves an encrypted copy of the
    vault key protected by Android Keystore. Fingerprint unlock uses a separate key
    that requires biometric authentication. Manual locking removes the saved timed
    session, and signing out removes both saved unlock methods. Read more about
    the design on our <a href="/security">security page</a> or inspect the
    <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier/tree/v0.1.3-android/android-app">Android source</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Get Authier on your phone</h2>
  <p>
    Head to the <a href="/download#android">Android download page</a> and select
    <strong>Set up with Obtainium</strong>. Install Obtainium if you need it,
    open the setup link again, and confirm the Authier configuration. Obtainium
    installs Authier from our signed GitHub releases and checks for future updates.
    A manual APK download is available on the same page.
  </p>
  <p>
    Already using the native Android app? Update it in place so your local vault
    stays intact. Then pick a lock timeout that suits your day and turn on
    fingerprint unlock. Your vault is ready to come with you.
  </p>
